DERIVED METRICS
Metric Name,Expression,Description
"IPC","RETIRED_INST / CYCLES_NOT_IN_HALT","The average number of retired instructions per CPU Cycle. The lower IPC value means the application consumes more cycles due to  cache misses, branch mispredictions, pipeline stalls, I/O or any other performance bottlenecks."
"CPI","CYCLES_NOT_IN_HALT / RETIRED_INST","The average number of CPU cycles consumed to retire an instruction. This metric is computed as the ratio of CYCLES_NOT_IN_HALT to RETIRED_INST event. The higher values means the application consumes more CPU cycles to retire an instruction due to high cache misses, branch mispredictions, pipeline stalls, I/O or any other bottlenecks. If the CPI values exceeds a threshold value, it will be highlighted in pink."
"RETIRED_BR_INST_MISP (PTI)","( RETIRED_BR_INST_MISP * 1000 ) / RETIRED_INST","The number of retired mispredicted branches per thousand retired instructions. Branch mispredictions incur significant performance penalty and this metric value should be reduced."
"%RETIRED_BR_INST_MISP","( RETIRED_BR_INST_MISP * 100 ) / RETIRED_BR_INST","The percentage of retired mispredicted branches with respect to the total number of retired branches."
"L1_DC_ACCESSES (PTI)","( L1_DC_ACCESSES_ALL * 1000 ) / RETIRED_INST","The number of load and store operations per thousand instructions. This counts the dispatch of single op that performs a memory load, dispatch of single op that performs a memory store, dispatch of a single op that performs a load from and store to the same memory address"
"L1_DC_MISSES (PTI)","( L2_CACHE_ACCESS_FROM_L1_DC_MISS * 1000 ) / RETIRED_INST","The number of L2 cache access requests due to L1 data cache misses, per thousand retired instructions. This L2 cache access requests also includes the hardware and software prefetches."
"%L1_DC_MISSES","( L2_CACHE_ACCESS_FROM_L1_DC_MISS * 100 ) / L1_DC_ACCESSES_ALL","The percentage of L2 cache access requests due to L1 data cache misses with respect to the total number of load and store operations. This also counts the hardware and software prefetches."
"L1_DEMAND_DC_REFILLS_LOCAL (PTI)","( L1_DEMAND_DC_REFILLS_LOCAL  * 1000 ) / RETIRED_INST","The number of demand data cache (DC) fills per thousand retired instructions. These demand DC fills are from all the data sources like Local L2/L3, CCX and DRAM."
"MISALIGNED_LOADS (PTI)","( MISALIGNED_LOADS * 1000 ) / RETIRED_INST","The number of misaligned loads per thousand retired instructions."


